# Directory-scoped override for this package's three headless unit tests
# (geometry_test.cpp, palette_logic_test.cpp, shadow_logic_test.cpp). They are plain
# C++20 programs with a tiny hand-rolled CHECK harness and large table-driven
# fixtures; running the root .clang-tidy Checks list against them produced several
# hundred warnings that trace back to a few test-only idioms, not to defects. Fixing
# the real findings (C-style casts, unchecked optionals, an uninitialised struct, a
# floating-point loop counter, a signed/unsigned comparison) was done in the files
# themselves; only the idioms below are relaxed.
#
# This override does NOT relax anything for the shipped plugin code (packages/
# kuura-decoration/src/, still governed by the root .clang-tidy's full Checks list
# and its HeaderFilterRegex) - the tests are not installed (PKGBUILD package()).
#
# Excluded here, with reasons (do not remove without understanding why):
#   -modernize-use-designated-initializers
#     Table rows such as `{"titleBarHeight", &Metrics::titleBarHeight, 23.0, 24.0,
#     64.0, 65.0}` and compact geometry fixtures `RectF{0, 0, 12, 12}` are read as
#     columns; naming every field on every row would triple the width of the tables
#     and hide the numbers that are the whole point of a boundary test.
#   -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays, -modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#     Those same fixture tables are `const Row rows[] = {...}` so the element count
#     is deduced; std::array would need an explicit size that must be kept in sync
#     with the number of rows by hand.
#   -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
#   -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index
#     Tests index vectors and arrays right after a CHECK of their size, or with a
#     loop index over a fixture table. A failing index here is itself a test
#     failure, so a bounds-checked accessor adds no safety (the same situation the
#     kuura-frost test override documents).
#   -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
#     g_checks / g_failures are the harness's two counters, incremented by the
#     CHECK macros and read by main() for the exit code and the summary line; a
#     test program has no other place to keep them without a fixture framework
#     this project deliberately does not depend on.
#   -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#     Test helpers such as makeParams(extent, offset, alpha, radius) take several
#     plain doubles named at every call site; strong types would only add noise.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
